cd /home/sfmqrb/git/rishe/data/verification/sources/refs && python3 - <<'EOF'
import re
t=open('SNS_pages.txt',encoding='utf-8',errors='replace').read()
pages=t.split('\f')
for i,p in enumerate(pages):
    for m in re.finditer(r'\bp[uūöo0][sšt]\w*', p):
        s=m.group(0)
        if len(s)>3:
            print(i, s, '|', p[max(0,m.start()-60):m.start()+80].replace('\n',' '))
EOF

cat > /home/sfmqrb/git/rishe/data/verification/page-408.json <<'JSONEOF'
{
  "pdf_page": 408,
  "book_page": 378,
  "verified_by": "claude-opus-5",
  "verified_on": "2026-09-13",
  "entries": [
    {
      "entry": 0,
      "root": "Pu 2",
      "verdict": "confirmed",
      "modern_form": "PIE *pu- / *p(h)u- 'to blow, blow up, swell' (imitative)",
      "note": "Pokorny IEW 847-848 'pū̆-1, peu-, pou- also phu-' meaning 'to blow, blow up'; Watkins/AHD 'pū-1. Also phū-. To blow, swell. Imitative root. [Pok. 1. pu- 847]'. Nourai's English gloss 'to blow, swell' is Watkins' wording verbatim, and POK:847 is the right page. The root is imitative/onomatopoeic, so Pokorny and Watkins both warn it has no fixed IE shape; the numbering 'Pu 2' is Nourai's own (Pokorny numbers it pū̆-1). Language label (Indo-European) and gloss are correct.",
      "note_fa": "ریشهٔ هندواروپایی آغازین *pu-/*p(h)u- «دمیدن، باد کردن، آماسیدن» است؛ پوکورنی آن را در صفحهٔ ۸۴۷ فرهنگ خود (IEW) زیر pū̆-1 آورده و واتکینز در پیوست ریشه‌های هندواروپایی فرهنگ AHD همان معنی «to blow, swell» را می‌دهد که نورایی واژه‌به‌واژه برگرفته است. این ریشه از گونهٔ ریشه‌های آوانمود (onomatopoeic) است و از همین رو صورت واحدی ندارد. برچسب زبانی و معنی ریشه در نمودار درست است؛ تنها شمارهٔ «۲» شماره‌گذاری خود نورایی است نه پوکورنی.",
      "sources": [
        "https://www.etymonline.com/word/pustule"
      ],
      "ref_check": [
        {"ref": "POK:847", "status": "supports", "note": "POK_full.txt, entry 'Root / lemma: pu-1, peu- pou- also phu-', 'Meaning: to blow, blow up', 'Page(s): 847-848'. The sub-section 'p(h)u-s-' on the same page gives 'Latin pussula, pustula \"bubble, vesicle, blister\"' and the sub-section 'p(h)u-k-' gives 'npers. pūk \"das Blasen (um Feuer anzufachen), Blasebalg\"' — i.e. exactly the two children Nourai draws."}
      ],
      "consulted": [
        {"src": "AHD", "where": "Watkins 1985, s.v. pū-1", "stance": "supports", "note": "'pu-1. Also phu-. To blow, swell. Imitative root. 1. Extended form *pus- in Latin pustula, a bubble, blister: PUSTULE. ... [Pok. 1. pu- 847.]' (AHD_watkins1985.txt line 872)."},
        {"src": "WLD", "where": "Bd. II p. 79 ff. (WLD_Bd2_pages.txt line 5351, 5403)", "stance": "supports", "note": "Walde-Pokorny Bd. II treats 'pū-, pu- \"blasen\"' with 'lat. pussula, pustula \"Blase, Bläschen\"' and cross-refers to 'u. pū- \"faulen, stinken\"' as a separate root — the same two-root split Nourai keeps (Pu 2 vs Pŭ 4)."},
        {"src": "IEC", "where": "Mann col./p. entry 'pūk- (phūk-)'", "stance": "supports", "note": "'pūk- (phūk-) \"swell, puff; swelling, puff\" ... Alb. cf. pucë, f. \"blister, pustule\" ... (Extn. in Gk. puknós ...)' (IEC.txt line 13733)."},
        {"src": "KLN", "where": "s.v. pustule", "stance": "supports", "note": "'from the I.-E. imitative base *pu-, *phu-, \"to blow, swell\", whence also OI. pupphusah, \"lung\" ... Gk. phusa, \"pair of bellows; breath, blast, wind, bubble\"' (KLN_1966.txt line 31142 area)."}
      ],
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "lang": "Persian",
          "words": "puk «پوک»",
          "verdict": "plausible",
          "derivation": "Pokorny does list New Persian pūk under this root, in the sub-section p(h)u-k-: 'npers. pūk \"das Blasen (um Feuer anzufachen), Blasebalg\", afgh. pūk \"a puff, a blast, the act of blowing\"' (IEW 847), taking it over from Horn, Grundriss no. 339 (p. 75). The phonology is the sticking point: Horn observes that Armenian pʿukʿ and Greek phūsa point to IE *ph-, while a New Persian p- initial would normally continue IE *p- and NP b- would continue IE *bh-, so 'die richtige neupersische Form muss būk sein'; Bartholomae (letter quoted by Horn) answered that tenuis/tenuis aspirata vary freely in the anlaut, and Hübschmann, Persische Studien no. 339 (p. 44), concludes 'Der Etymologie wegen ist np. pūk nicht zu verdächtigen'. The problem with Nourai's node is the GLOSS: every source that puts pūk under *pu- glosses it 'blowing (to fan a fire), bellows, puff', not 'empty'. NP پوک 'hollow, empty, porous' (Steingass; Wiktionary) is either a semantic extension of the same word ('blown up' > 'puffed up' > 'hollow, with nothing inside') — a step none of the cited authorities actually takes — or a separate expressive formation. Root family right, gloss unsupported: plausible.",
          "derivation_fa": "«پوک» در فرهنگ‌های امروزی به معنی «تهی، میان‌خالی، بی‌مغز» است، اما آنچه پوکورنی (ص ۸۴۷) و هرن (بند ۳۳۹، ص ۷۵) زیر این ریشه آورده‌اند «پوک» به معنی «دمیدن (برای برافروختن آتش)، دَم آهنگری» است، با همریشهٔ ارمنی pʿukʿ «دَم» و پشتوی pūk. هرن هشدار می‌دهد که از نظر آوایی صورت درست فارسی باید «بوک» باشد، چون «پ» فارسی نو دنبالهٔ *p هندواروپایی و «ب» دنبالهٔ *bh است؛ ولی بارتولومه و هوبشمان (مطالعات فارسی، بند ۳۳۹، ص ۴۴) این تردید را نپذیرفته‌اند و هوبشمان می‌نویسد ریشه‌شناسی np. pūk جای گمان ندارد. پس پیوند واژه با ریشهٔ «دمیدن» پذیرفتنی است، اما معنی «تهی» که نورایی می‌دهد در هیچ‌یک از منابع یادشده نیامده و تحول معنایی «باد کرده ← میان‌تهی» فرضی است؛ ادعا با احتیاط پذیرفتنی است.",
          "sources": [
            "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%D9%BE%D9%88%DA%A9"
          ],
          "ref_check": [
            {"ref": "POK:847", "status": "partial", "note": "POK_full.txt, 'pu-1 ... Page(s): 847-848', sub-section 'p(h)u-k-': 'npers. pūk \"das blast (um fire anzufachen), bellows\", afgh. pu, puk \"a puff, a blast, the act of blowing\"' (OCR). Pokorny has the word under this root but glosses it 'blowing, bellows', not 'empty'."},
            {"ref": "HRN:75", "status": "partial", "note": "HRN.txt leaf 96 = printed p. 75, no. 339: 'pūk, pŭk: das Blasen (um Feuer anzufachen), Blasebalg. gr. φῦσα ... arm. pʿuk ... Die richtige neupersische Form muss būk sein.' Horn's page is exactly the one cited, but his gloss is 'blowing/bellows' and he flags a phonological difficulty; footnote 2 even asks whether the dictionaries' meaning 'Brennholz' for np. pūk is merely guessed."}
          ],
          "consulted": [
            {"src": "HUB", "where": "Persische Studien no. 339, p. 44 (HUB.txt line 1469)", "stance": "supports", "note": "'339. Der Etymologie wegen ist np. puk nicht zu verdächtigen. Vgl. afgh. pu, puk \"a puff, a blast, the act of blowing\", pukai \"a puff, inflating\" ... Lies φῦσα.' — Hübschmann defends the etymology but again only for the sense 'puff, blowing'."},
            {"src": "IEC", "where": "Mann, s.v. pūk- (phūk-) (IEC.txt line 13733)", "stance": "partial", "note": "'pūk- (phūk-) \"swell, puff; swelling, puff\"' — the root-form is there (with Lith. pūkas, Alb. pucë 'blister'), but Mann lists no Persian reflex."},
            {"src": "ARY", "where": "ARY_pages.txt, searched پوک", "stance": "silent", "note": "Aryanpur's Persian IE-roots dictionary has no entry پوک (grep of ARY_pages.txt for 'پوک' returns only the پوسیدن material)."},
            {"src": "Wiktionary", "where": "en.wiktionary.org/wiki/پوک", "stance": "partial", "note": "Persian پوک (puk) is glossed simply 'hollow', citing Steingass 1892; no etymology is offered, so the 'empty' sense is attested but unetymologised."}
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "lang": "Latin",
          "words": "pustula",
